r the implementation root |\\n|---|---|\\n| Task IDs and documents | `tasks/<task-id>/` |\\n| Results and evidence | `runs/<task-id>/<agent-run-id>/` |\\n| Native turns | `native/<session-id>/<turn-id>.jsonl` (Codex) or `.json` (OpenCode) |\\n| Reports | `reports/` |\\n\\n## Assignment format\\n\\nApply to the assignment line sent during handoff.\\n\\n- Fill in the implementation name, source task ID and recipient role.\\n- Put the assignment marker at the start of its own line.\\n- Use the optional `purpose` field to describe the assignment.\\n- Keep the assignment for follow-ups unless explicitly retagged.\\n- Keep replacement workers' native identities separate.\\n- Use `supervisor` / `orchestration` for Supervisor turns and `validator` / `validation` for final validation.\\n- Emit your own assignment line in commentary after allocation or resume.\\n\\n```text\\nAGENTIC_WORKFLOW {\\\"implementation\\\":\\\"001_todolist\\\",\\\"task\\\":\\\"01_business_logic\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"implementer\\\"}\\n```\\n# Document style\\n\\nApply in every role only when writing or editing project documents, including workflow documentation.\\nSource code, code comments and docstrings are outside this policy's scope.\\n\\n- Describe workflows in this order: Context → Inputs → Effects → Outputs → Next.\\n- Omit Next when unnecessary.\\n- Format guideline sections like [Engineering guidelines](GUIDELINES.md): short title, applicability sentence and flat imperative bullets.\\n- Write one short, single-sentence rule per list item.\\n- Keep related details together when the rule remains short.\\n- Use bullets for rules and numbered lists only for action sequences.\\n- Separate procedural sections from guideline sections.\\n- Link to each shared policy rule's authoritative home instead of repeating it.\\n\\n## Workflow contract\\n\\nApply when changing workflow behavior or its documentation.\\n\\n- Treat [WORKFLOW.md](../WORKFLOW.md) as the authoritative source of workflow behavior.\\n- Update it whenever workflow behavior changes.\\n- Express changes as brief statements of core responsibilities and outcomes.\\n- Keep procedures, state formats and implementation details in role documents or policies.\\n- Derive complete execution duties in role documents from it.\\n- Keep those documents free of references back to the contract.\\n- Keep derived instructions consistent with the workflow contract.\\n# Project memory\\n\\nApply during ordinary planning, implementation and memory handoffs.\\n\\n- For ordinary work, read `<project-root>/.agentic-workflow/memory/index.md`, then only relevant `entries/*.md`.\\n- Treat a missing index as no saved notes.\\n- Follow current requirements and repository facts over conflicting memory.\\n- Check advice that may be outdated.\\n- Do not search unrelated tasks or conversations.\\n- Save only useful, source-backed lessons when work finishes or is blocked.\\n- Merge duplicate notes and correct outdated advice.\\n- Use ordinary Markdown without requiring metadata.\\n- Write short hints that help later workers find relevant notes.\\n- Leave out transcripts, progress logs, guesses, secrets and copied configuration.\\n- Pass relevant note paths to later workers doing ordinary work.\\n- As Supervisor, pass paths without reading detailed notes.\\n- Do not read memory or copies of it as a reviewer, validator or reconstruction worker.\\n---\\nname: test-audit\\ndescription: \\\"Writing/changing/reviewing/sweeping tests: reject duplicate or implementation-coupled proof; remove test-only production seams.\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Test Audit\\n\\n- Authoring gates every new/changed test.\\n- Audits: remove low-value proof in coherent owner batches; never chase deletion counts.\\n- Whole-subsystem campaign: read [CAMPAIGN.md](CAMPAIGN.md) first.\\n\\n## Authoring gate\\n\\nBefore adding test, answer:\\n\\n1. Protected observable behavior, invariant, or independent contract?\\n2. Credible regression that makes it fail?\\n3. Why existing proof misses it? Each contract: one primary owner at strongest\\n   boundary. Another layer needs distinct transport/lifecycle risk. Extend\\n   tables/shared fixtures; consolidate repeated setup.\\n4. Export, flag, wrapper, injection hook with no production caller needed?\\n   Move proof to real boundary instead.\\n\\n- Use [boundary and cost guide](../../../docs/help/testing/writing-tests.md).\\n- Regressions must fail pre-fix for intended reason, pass after repair; report\\n  unavailable baseline proof.\\n- One owner regression covers bug; never replay at every crossed layer.\\n- Behavior-preserving refactors should not break test.\\n\\n## Junk patterns\\n\\n- Reject self-comparisons, copied inventories, source greps,\\n  implementation/call-shape assertions, duplicate contracts, test-only seams,\\n  subject-generated expected values, mocks supplying asserted behavior.\\n- Fixtures must not fabricate owner receipts/order or claim persistence path\\n  never writes.\\n- Negative controls must fail at intended guard; names must match exercised behavior.\\n- Auditing candidates: use [full checklist](references/audit.md#junk-patterns).\\n\\n## Retention bar\\n\\n- Keep independent API, SDK, protocol, config, migration, storage, security,\\n  platform, default, prompt-byte, generated-language, package, release,\\n  architecture, observable-ordering contracts. Static/slow ≠ disposable.\\n- Source inspection must survive identifier-only refactors and guard independent\\n  user-facing contract.\\n- Baseline failures may be bugs to repair, not tests to delete.\\n\\n## Audit and validation\\n\\n- Before audit edit: read [candidate evidence and workflow](references/audit.md#candidate-evidence);\\n  inspect full owners/callers/history; record remaining proof before deletion.\\n- Delete obsolete production seams with tests; never optimize for deletion counts.\\n- Follow [proof policy](../openclaw-testing/SKILL.md#proof-policy); preserve active\\n  Vitest checkouts; run owner/sibling proof + changed checks; then autoreview.\\n- Report causes, retained contracts, proof/cost, production versus test LOC,\\n  follow-ups. Commit/push/land only with task authority.\\n\"}"
    },
