 — message content.\\n- `client_sent_at: ClientTimestampInput` — optional sender timestamp.\\n\\nExample request:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"send\\\",\\n  \\\"correlation_id\\\": \\\"629a6d45-679d-4e09-8b3a-d6d779ab415c\\\",\\n  \\\"data\\\": {\\n    \\\"recipient\\\": \\\"bob\\\",\\n    \\\"text\\\": \\\"Hi Bob\\\",\\n    \\\"client_sent_at\\\": \\\"2026-11-08T12:00:00Z\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nIf Bob is offline, the server correlates the error with that request.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"error\\\",\\n  \\\"correlation_id\\\": \\\"629a6d45-679d-4e09-8b3a-d6d779ab415c\\\",\\n  \\\"data\\\": {\\n    \\\"message\\\": \\\"Recipient is offline\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### ack\\n\\n- `message_id: UUID` — message being acknowledged.\\n- `recipient_received_at: ClientTimestampInput` — optional recipient timestamp.\\n\\nExample request acknowledging a received message:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"ack\\\",\\n  \\\"correlation_id\\\": \\\"b4a0fa95-9c1c-472e-98ae-42fdc01c8aa7\\\",\\n  \\\"data\\\": {\\n    \\\"message_id\\\": \\\"6ab59054-8e3c-4b20-9a11-32922d384f68\\\",\\n    \\\"recipient_received_at\\\": \\\"2026-11-08T12:01:00Z\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Server events\\n\\nUse these event names and payloads for replies and notifications.\\n\\n### login_ok\\n\\nReply to a successful login with `data` matching the [users contract](storage.md#users).\\n\\n### message_accepted\\n\\nReply to an accepted send with `data` matching the [messages contract](storage.md#messages).\\nAcceptance confirms storage only; delivery remains unconfirmed without a `delivery_receipt`.\\n\\n### message_received\\n\\nNotify the recipient of an incoming message with `data` matching the [messages contract](storage.md#messages).\\n\\n### delivery_receipt\\n\\nNotify the original sender of a valid acknowledgment if still connected, using these fields inside `data`.\\n\\n- `message_id: UUID`.\\n- `recipient_received_at: UtcTimestamp | 0`.\\n- `server_ack_received_at: UtcTimestamp`.\\n\\nA valid `ack` produces a delivery receipt for the original sender without a separate success reply to the acknowledging client.\\n\\n### error\\n\\nReply to the client whose request failed validation or was rejected, including an invalid `ack`, using this field inside `data`.\\n\\n- `message: string`.\\n# <Role/run> — result\\n\\nOmit inapplicable fields. Keep forwarded independent-check inputs within [Checks](../policies/CHECKS.md). Document-only results describe document validation, not app execution.\\n\\n- **Scope and candidate:** <Sources, applicable acceptance, candidate location/revision and dependencies.>\\n- **Role and status:** <Assigned mode; PASS, FAIL, BLOCKED or NOT_RUN; rationale and unfinished work.>\\n- **Model routing:** <Profile, reason, requested model/reasoning, observed settings if available, fallback or known mismatch.>\\n- **Checks:** <Requirement ID, command/method, working directory, exit/outcome and evidence. For manual checks, authority and inspected artifact. Separate execution from coverage and cleanup errors from primary failures.>\\n- **Findings and resolutions:** <Requirement, expected/observed behavior, reproduction, repair and remaining findings. Preserve useful failures.>\\n- **Coverage and blockers:** <Substitutes, skipped checks, gaps and required decisions.>\\n- **Independent checks:** <Fresh session/result paths and prior fixes. Keep review findings distinct from the Supervisor's acceptance decision.>\\n- **Assembled app:** <Final execution evidence or why incomplete; omit for task-only/document results.>\\n- **Usage:** <Derived aggregate reports when available, missing counters and coverage limits, including repairs and blocked work.>\\n- **Reconstruction:** <Allowed/retained inputs, target changes, actual isolation controls, exclusions/leakage and limits.>\\n\"}"
