        "type": "input_text",
        "text": "{\"chunk_id\":\"b6cdab\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000010149,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2376,\"output\":\"<!-- agentic-workflow:start -->\\n# Agentic Workflow\\n\\n- Before planning, changing or reviewing code, tests or tooling, read\\n  [Engineering guidelines](agentic-workflow/policies/GUIDELINES.md).\\n- For specification implementation, read\\n  [Workflow entry points](agentic-workflow/AGENTS.md) and act as Supervisor.\\n- For document authoring or workflow maintenance, read those entry points\\n  and act as Planner.\\n- Before authoring or editing project documents,\\n  read [Document style](agentic-workflow/policies/DOCUMENT_STYLE.md), regardless of role.\\n- Ordinary planning and implementation follows\\n  [Project memory](agentic-workflow/policies/MEMORY.md); implement ordinary work directly.\\n- Keep project inputs, application code, memory and execution evidence\\n  outside `agentic-workflow/`.\\n<!-- agentic-workflow:end -->\\n\\nFor ordinary work, apply the guidelines, run relevant checks, inspect the diff and\\nreport results. Formal workflow artifacts and roles are optional unless requested.\\nPlan-only requests stop at the plan; preserve explicit approval requirements.\\nWorkflow helpers may be changed when workflow/tooling implementation is requested.\\nAdvice/tooling work uses requested files and relevant references without task-history\\ndiscovery. For the repository's todolist eval, read [the eval guide](evals/README.md).\\n# Engineering guidelines\\n\\nRead before planning, production code, tests, tooling, review or repairs.\\n\\n- Separate state and logic.\\n- Use classes that mix state and logic only when required.\\n- Localize side effects.\\n- Keep each module's top-level flow clear and functional.\\n- Prefer small, Unix-like modules.\\n- Give each module a public API with few responsibilities.\\n- Prioritize public behaviour tests.\\n- Internal tests can add useful coverage.\\n- Prefer real infrastructure.\\n- Justify mocks under [Checks](CHECKS.md).\\n- Compose larger structures from small modules.\\n- Test public behaviour for every eligible module.\\n- Test public contracts specified in the task.\\n- Add validations, locks, checksums and manifests only when needed or explicitly requested.\\n- Do not create backwards-compatible functionality unless explicitly requested.\\n- Use simple language in comments and documents.\\n- Avoid dense jargon and stock AI phrasing.\\n# Reviewer\\n\\n## Review a task\\n\\n- Context:\\n  - Read [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md), [Checks](../policies/CHECKS.md) and [Records](../policies/RECORDS.md).\\n- Inputs:\\n  - Requirements, acceptance, candidate and permitted evidence.\\n  - Supervisor confirms review boundary paused.\\n- Effects:\\n  - Apply Checks' fresh-context, permitted-input and inspection-order rules.\\n  - Check implementation against acceptance, public API contracts and expected scenarios.\\n  - Check code and acceptance against every applicable requirement.\\n  - Find omissions, weakened expectations and unjustified constraints.\\n  - Check interactions, unintended changes and prior findings.\\n  - Report missing or conflicting contracts.\\n  - Inspect public API unit and integration tests.\\n  - Check scenario coverage and independent expected outcomes.\\n  - Assess internal tests and mock justifications under Checks.\\n  - Accept internal tests and mocks when they provide useful evidence.\\n  - Request stronger tests for concrete coverage gaps.\\n  - Check that each test layer covers a distinct risk.\\n  - Assess guideline exceptions.\\n  - Check for test-only production hooks.\\n  - Run relevant checks.\\n  - Reproduce findings where feasible.\\n  - Keep requirements and code unchanged.\\n  - Report candidate changes to Implementer and Supervisor.\\n  - Apply Checks' recheck rules.\\n  - Save the [result](../templates/result.md).\\n  - Report blockers promptly.\\n- Outputs:\\n  - Result and available usage paths.\\n  - Include status, source-linked findings, reproductions, verified fixes and coverage limits.\\n  - Identify public API contract defects and test gaps.\\n- Next:\\n  - Return findings and result to Implementer.\\n  - Supervisor releases paused writers.\\n# Agentic Workflow\\n\\nRead the context for your action:\\n\\n| Action | Context |\\n|---|---|\\n| Implement specifications, including one task | [SUPERVISOR.md](roles/SUPERVISOR.md), enter as Supervisor |\\n| Update or repair an existing app against revised specifications | [Supervisor reconciliation](roles/SUPERVISOR.md#reconcile-an-existing-implementation) |\\n| Coordinate tasks | [SUPERVISOR.md](roles/SUPERVISOR.md) |\\n| Plan or edit documents/workflow | [PLANNER.md](roles/PLANNER.md) |\\n| Implement a task | [IMPLEMENTER.md](roles/IMPLEMENTER.md) |\\n| Review a task | [REVIEWER.md](roles/REVIEWER.md) |\\n| Validate the app | [VALIDATOR.md](roles/VALIDATOR.md) |\\n| Resolve project files | [BUNDLE.md](policies/BUNDLE.md) |\\n| Define or assess checks | [CHECKS.md](policies/CHECKS.md) |\\n| Hand off, save or resume work | [RECORDS.md](policies/RECORDS.md) |\\n| Ordinary planning/implementation | [MEMORY.md](policies/MEMORY.md) |\\n| Rebuild without prior implementation | [RECONSTRUCTION.md](policies/RECONSTRUCTION.md), before any role starts |\\n| Review workflow documents | [WORKFLOW_REVIEW.md](guides/WORKFLOW_REVIEW.md) |\\n| Install or check the package/optional skills | [README.md](README.md) |\\n| Inspect traces or usage | [TRACING.md](guides/TRACING.md) |\\n\\nEvery role reads [GUIDELINES.md](policies/GUIDELINES.md), resolves [MODELS.md](policies/MODELS.md#routing-source),\\nand applies its context documents. Follow conditional references when applicable.\\nBefore authoring or editing project documents,\\nread and apply [Document style](policies/DOCUMENT_STYLE.md), regardless of role.\\nKeep project inputs, code, memory and execution evidence outside this package.\\n\\nTemplates: [project inputs](policies/BUNDLE.md), [plan](templates/plan.md),\\n[acceptance](templates/acceptance.md), [result](templates/result.md).\\n---\\nname: test-audit\\ndescription: \\\"Writing/changing/reviewing/sweeping tests: reject duplicate or implementation-coupled proof; remove test-only production seams.\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Test Audit\\n\\n- Authoring gates every new/changed test.\\n- Audits: remove low-value proof in coherent owner batches; never chase deletion counts.\\n- Whole-subsystem campaign: read [CAMPAIGN.md](CAMPAIGN.md) first.\\n\\n## Authoring gate\\n\\nBefore adding test, answer:\\n\\n1. Protected observable behavior, invariant, or independent contract?\\n2. Credible regression that makes it fail?\\n3. Why existing proof misses it? Each contract: one primary owner at strongest\\n   boundary. Another layer needs distinct transport/lifecycle risk. Extend\\n   tables/shared fixtures; consolidate repeated setup.\\n4. Export, flag, wrapper, injection hook with no production caller needed?\\n   Move proof to real boundary instead.\\n\\n- Use [boundary and cost guide](../../../docs/help/testing/writing-tests.md).\\n- Regressions must fail pre-fix for intended reason, pass after repair; report\\n  unavailable baseline proof.\\n- One owner regression covers bug; never replay at every crossed layer.\\n- Behavior-preserving refactors should not break test.\\n\\n## Junk patterns\\n\\n- Reject self-comparisons, copied inventories, source greps,\\n  implementation/call-shape assertions, duplicate contracts, test-only seams,\\n  subject-generated expected values, mocks supplying asserted behavior.\\n- Fixtures must not fabricate owner receipts/order or claim persistence path\\n  never writes.\\n- Negative controls must fail at intended guard; names must match exercised behavior.\\n- Auditing candidates: use [full checklist](references/audit.md#junk-patterns).\\n\\n## Retention bar\\n\\n- Keep independent API, SDK, protocol, config, migration, storage, security,\\n  platform, default, prompt-byte, generated-language, package, release,\\n  architecture, observable-ordering contracts. Static/slow ≠ disposable.\\n- Source inspection must survive identifier-only refactors and guard independent\\n  user-facing contract.\\n- Baseline failures may be bugs to repair, not tests to delete.\\n\\n## Audit and validation\\n\\n- Before audit edit: read [candidate evidence and workflow](references/audit.md#candidate-evidence);\\n  inspect full owners/callers/history; record remaining proof before deletion.\\n- Delete obsolete production seams with tests; never optimize for deletion counts.\\n- Follow [proof policy](../openclaw-testing/SKILL.md#proof-policy); preserve active\\n  Vitest checkouts; run owner/sibling proof + changed checks; then autoreview.\\n- Report causes, retained contracts, proof/cost, production versus test LOC,\\n  follow-ups. Commit/push/land only with task authority.\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/runs/01_api/review/result.md\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/tasks/01_api/acceptance.md\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/tasks/01_api/plan.md\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/runs/01_api/implementation/container-r1.txt\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/runs/01_api/implementation/docker-build-r1.txt\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/runs/01_api/implementation/pytest-r1.txt\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/runs/01_api/implementation/ruff.txt\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/runs/01_api/implementation/result.md\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/runs/01_api/implementation/docker-build.txt\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/runs/01_api/implementation/container.txt\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/runs/01_api/implementation/container_smoke.py\\n.agentic-workflow/records/001_chat/runs/01_api/implementation/pytest.txt\\nspecs/spec_chat/verification.md\\nspecs/spec_chat/task_order.md\\nspecs/spec_chat/project.md\\nspecs/spec_chat/contracts/storage.md\\nspecs/spec_chat/contracts/websocket.md\\nspecs/spec_chat/.gitkeep\\nspecs/spec_chat